=== (A4) non-Gaussian noise: recombined amplitude is controlled by anti-concentration at 1 photon ===
 circular Gaussian, V=50                       var=49.3 |E alpha|=0.941 : recombination prob ~ 0.0016 ; <a>_rec = -0.091-0.186i (Gaussian formula 2Psi/(2+V) = 0.0367)
 lognormal multiplicative, E|W|^2=51           var=23.7 |E alpha|=1.021 : recombination prob ~ 0.7403 ; <a>_rec = 0.266+0.000i (Gaussian formula 2Psi/(2+V) = 0.0793)
 lognormal amp x uniform phase                 var=63.5 |E alpha|=0.125 : recombination prob ~ 0.6870 ; <a>_rec = 0.006+0.001i (Gaussian formula 2Psi/(2+V) = 0.0038)
 90% quiet (alpha=Psi) + 10% Gaussian V=500    var=50.1 |E alpha|=1.026 : recombination prob ~ 0.8158 ; <a>_rec = 1.000-0.000i (Gaussian formula 2Psi/(2+V) = 0.0394)

=== (A5) linear combination of unitaries ===
 (1/sqrt2) 1 + (i/sqrt2) sigma_z unitary? ||W^dag W - 1|| = 2.2e-16 ; but the mean (1+sigma_z)/2 = diag(1,0) is not.
 convex 0.5 U0 + 0.5 U1: min singular value 0.6242 (<1, so never unitary unless U0 = U1 up to nothing)
